rust	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-17T01:44:20.6468317Z   BODY: Closes #1219
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	## For humans
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	While you type a message in a thread on the phone, a new message from the orchestrator (or its "working" pill starting or ending) no longer takes the cursor out of the box.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	The keyboard stays open, the cursor and any selection stay where they were, and the next key lands in the message.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	## What changed
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- Root cause: the server sends a `merge` op on the composer block (`say`) when a turn starts or ends (`working` changes). Its block key changed, so `morph` replaced the whole composer element and the focused textarea left the DOM (blur, caret reset, the iOS keyboard closes).
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- `web/src/blocks.ts`: when the composer block changes, `same()` now hands the new block to the live composer, which redraws in place. Its textarea and its row are never detached (`around` swaps only their siblings). An unchanged composer still goes through the old path, so the repaint test's "no node removed" check still holds.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- `web/dist/board.js` rebuilt (`npm --prefix web run build`).
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- Test: `crates/cli/tests/ui/compose.mjs` + `page_drafts::a_new_orchestrator_message_while_typing_keeps_the_composer_focused_with_its_caret_and_text` (390 px). Focus the box, type, select 4..6, then the stream sends `working` on and a reply card with `working: null`. It asserts the same textarea node, focus, caret [4,6], text kept, no blur, and that the next key lands in the box. Added to the ui-webkit trigger regex in ci.yml.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	## Evidence (head cddb409170ded63e606b71dc06e3af8b20980003)
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	WebKit isn't installed on the lane host, and lanes may not install browsers. So I ran the same tests locally on Playwright 1.63 **Chromium**, swapping `webkit` for `chromium` in the test scripts locally only (not committed). CI's ui-webkit job runs them on WebKit.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- Base + commit 1 (5f13c5e1): `cargo test --locked --test page_drafts a_new_orchestrator…` → exit 101. Failing output: `"after":{"blurs":1,"caret":[14,14],"focus":false,"same":false,"value":"half a thought"}`, typed `"half a thought"` (the key was lost).
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- Head: `cargo test --locked --test page_drafts` → exit 0 (3 passed: the new test, repaint, drafts).
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- Head: `cargo test --locked --test threads_tab webkit -- --test-threads=1` → 7 passed, plus `two_panes…` rerun with duo.mjs swapped too → exit 0.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- `npx tsc --noEmit` exit 0, `npm run lint` exit 0, `cargo fmt --check` exit 0.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- `drover arch-check`: 2 violations, both already on staging and not from this PR: `serve.rs` is over its size baseline, and `just` isn't available on this host.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	src/ net +0 Rust (budget n/a); web/src +13 lines (soft budget): the composer's in-place redraw.
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	## Not verified
rust	UNKNOWN STEP	- Real WebKit and the owner's phone check (the keyboard staying open on iOS).
